data: {"level":1,"reviewed":{"level":1,"label":"concept","text":"Planning a test is a trade-off between four numbers: the baseline, the effect you care about, the false\npositive rate `alpha` and the power `1 − beta`. The sample size needed is the one that makes the difference\nbetween the two rates, divided by its standard error, large enough. The standard error has two versions here:\none under \"no difference\" and one under \"the effect is real\"."},"hints_note":null}

